  "@id": "https://pices-data.github.io/odis/records/zenodo-23570891.jsonld",
  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Ship of Opportunity - Canada to Australia, 1981-present",
  "description": "Data from merchant ships travelling between British Columbia and Australia, from 1981 to 1988 (Lillooet), 1997-1998 (Western Hawk), 1998-1999 (Australian Current), and 1999-2000, continuing (Packing). Data collected include total carbon dioxide, alkalinity(after 1997), nutrients, chlorophyll a (after 1997), carbon-13 in seawater, atmospheric carbon dioxide (PCO2), and atmospheric carbon-13. Underway measurements include position, time, temperature and salinity\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: Constructing models of Pacific Ocean carbon cycling; air-sea exchange, monitoring long term changes in the Pacific Ocean, tracking water masses in the ocean, El Nino monitoring\n\nSupplemental information: Risk Justification: Custodian will be leaving soon and has a large quantity of data not secured in a regional data centre. Risk of Loss: High Impact Justification: Time series of 5 to 10 years Impact of Loss: Medium Recommended Action: Obtain access to data, bring data to archives",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23570892",
